%I A401332 #8 Oct 28 2026 22:47:49
%S A401332 0,10,11,13,17,20,24,30,32,40,50,59,60,70,74,80,82,90,100,110,111,113,
%T A401332 117,120,124,130,132,140,150,159,160,170,174,180,182,190,200,210,211,
%U A401332 213,217,220,224,230,232,240,250,259,260,270,274,280,282,290,300,310
%N A401332 Numbers k such that the units digit of 3*k equals the tens digit of k^3.
%C A401332 The sequence is periodic modulo 100, with 18 qualifying residue classes: {0, 10, 11, 13, 17, 20, 24, 30, 32, 40, 50, 59, 60, 70, 74, 80, 82, 90} (mod 100). Its natural density is 18/100 = 9/50.
%C A401332 This is the case m = 3 of the family defined by floor(k^m/10) mod 10 = (m*k) mod 10, extending the case m = 2 in A399563.
%F A401332 a(n) = a(n-18) + 100 for n > 18.
%e A401332 For k = 13, 13^3 = 2197 (tens digit 9) and 3*13 = 39 (units digit 9), so 13 is in the sequence.
%e A401332 For k = 17, 17^3 = 4913 (tens digit 1) and 3*17 = 51 (units digit 1), so 17 is in the sequence.
%e A401332 For k = 12, 12^3 = 1728 (tens digit 2) and 3*12 = 36 (units digit 6), so 12 is not in the sequence.
%t A401332 Select[Range[0, 500], Mod[Quotient[#^3, 10], 10] == Mod[3*#, 10] &]
%o A401332 (Python) [n for n in range(501) if (n**3 // 10) % 10 == (3*n) % 10]
%Y A401332 Cf. A399563 (the case m = 2).
%K A401332 nonn,base,easy,new
%O A401332 1,2
%A A401332 _Yu-Wen Wang_ and Gwo-Haur Hwang, Oct 21 2026
